It is a very good and interesting game. In my opinion storywise it is way better then all new batman movies. Gameplaywise it is a good mix of various genres. Some stealth, some fighting, etc. On a hardest difficulty level main story and approximately 60% of secrets took ~22 hours. However, I certainly spend at least 20 percent replaying some difficult bosses and locations.
Advantages of this game are as follows:
1) Really interesting and engaging storyline;
2) Joker's voice most certainly represents one of the best voice performances;
3) Mostly openworld gameplay with possibility to continue exploring after main story;
4) Enjoyable combat system;
5) Good stealth system;
6) Very good transitions between various challenges in levels;
7) Despite the fact that all the story happens within one facility it always changes, thus, allowing one rediscover all locations from new perspectives;
8) In most locations there are several ways how one can fight enemies: using stealth approach or directly or even using a bit of this and a bit of that, etc.
9) Lots of various challenges to extend play value of the game and various trophies and secrets which enrich story with information on various characters, their stories, etc.
Though I certainly recommend this game, it has some minor cons worth mentioning:
1) Difficulty of swarms of minor enemies is higher than that of one or even two larger enemies. For example, It was not a big deal for me to defeat two titans while it is sometimes was quite tricky to defeat a dozen of minor enemies.
2) Bosses do not give you much variation in the way you can fight them. Batarang, dodge and then beat the crap out of them and variations on the same theme. It would be great if there would be a stealth or other alternative way to defeat bosses;
3) You get locked in certain locations until you finish the challenge there. Most of the time it is not a problem as one anyway would go only forwards. However, sometimes you enter a room and you realize that you have to fight 10-15 small enemies. If you will attempt to leave batman says "I can not leave before I do that and that" and that is it. Even on the highest difficulty level all such situations manageable, but sometimes it just makes you think that you should have gathered a bit more XP before going there.
4) Quite linear story. No choices or almost no choices. There is some variation in the way how you can approach some sub-missions. Whom save first someone here or someone there, etc. More importantly, these choices do not affect story at all. Otherwise it is quite linear. Therefore, from the main storyline perspective there is not much replay value. Having said that story is quite good and even without variation I would play it again after some time.
5) Batman is incapable of continuous long distance flights. This is solved in sequel :) . There Batman is flying even better then superman ;) .
Taking all aforementioned into account I like this game very much and would recommend it.

